# Fill simulator (`backtest/simulate_fills.py`)

Walks real 1-minute OHLC from each v8.8 signal. Outcomes are `win`,
`loss`, `no_fill_never_traded`, `no_fill_timeout`, `no_fill_50pct`,
and `no_fill_by_eod`. `realized_R` comes from the simulated exit,
**not** from `target_R`. Do not invent a fill.

SMT_IN_FVG is a market fill at the confirmation-bar **close**. That
bar's high/low already printed, so stop/target checks start on the
**next** bar. FVG_AFTER_SMT is a limit at the FVG 50% level; the fill
bar itself is eligible for stop/target after the limit trades.

## Touch logic — high/low, never close

Stop and target are hit when the bar **high** or **low** reaches the
level. Never use the close to decide a stop or target.

- LONG stop: `low <= stop_loss`. LONG target: `high >= take_profit`.
- SHORT stop: `high >= stop_loss`. SHORT target: `low <= take_profit`.
- A bar that opens through the stop is a loss; a bar that opens through
  the target is a win. Close is used only as the SMT_IN_FVG fill price
  and as the flatten price on `no_fill_by_eod`.

## Same-bar ambiguity — stop first

If both stop and target trade in the same bar, the stop is assumed hit
**first** (conservative default). 1-minute OHLC has no intra-bar order,
so this is a stated choice, not a data fact. Do not flip it to
target-first to improve historical R.

## FVG_AFTER_SMT limit cancels — Juliana 8.7-era trading notes

These two cancels are **stated rules from Juliana's own 8.7-era
trading notes**, not arbitrary simulator knobs. A later cleanup must
not drop them because they look like extra filters. Do not fake a fill.

1. **Time (`no_fill_timeout`):** if the limit is not filled within
   **20 minutes** of the FVG identification bar (`fvg_bar`), cancel.
   The bar at elapsed == 20 minutes is already too late, even if that
   bar would have traded the limit.
2. **Price (`no_fill_50pct`):** if, before the limit fills, price
   reaches **50% of the distance to `take_profit`** (bar high for
   LONG, bar low for SHORT), cancel. The setup has already moved
   toward the target without filling the limit; chasing it is not
   the rule.

If the limit is never reached at all before session end (and the
20-minute mark never arrives), that is `no_fill_never_traded`. Do
not lump timeout / 50% / never-traded into a single `no_fill`.

Same-bar: if the limit fills on a bar that also prints the 50%
level, take the fill (the 50% cancel is only while unfilled).

## Session-end handling

Default: a filled trade that hits neither stop nor target by session
close is `no_fill_by_eod`, flattened at that last in-window bar's
close. Scanner session windows: NY Morning 08:00–10:30 ET, NY
Afternoon 13:00–15:00 ET. `session_end_utc()` always uses those two
closes — it is the unfilled-limit wait cap and the default flatten.

**NY Morning exception (stated rule):** a trade **entered after
09:45 ET** (`flatten_end_utc`) closes at **11:00 ET** instead of the
normal 10:30 NY Morning cutoff. "Entered" is the fill bar (confirmation
close for SMT_IN_FVG; limit-fill bar for FVG_AFTER_SMT). 09:45 itself
is not after 09:45 and still flattens at 10:30.

**This extended cutoff does not apply to NY Afternoon signals.**
Afternoon remains 15:00. There is no analogue (no "entered after
14:15, close at 15:30"). Do not copy the 11:00 exception onto
afternoon trades. Unfilled limits never wait past the normal
session close, even in the morning.

## Known gaps — disclose on every report

Any report, CSV, or summary produced from this simulator **must
disclose these three gaps**. They are not implied by a win rate.

1. **Partial exits are not simulated.** No codified rule exists for
   scaling out. Every fill is all-or-nothing at stop, target, or
   session flatten.
2. **Concurrent-trade limits are not enforced.** Policy is undecided
   (how many overlapping positions are allowed). The simulator will
   take every signal independently, including two that are live at
   the same time.
3. **5m-opposing-SMT blocking is not implemented.** That filter is in
   an evidence-gathering stage. Do not treat simulator results as
   "already blocked on opposing 5m SMT."

Do not silently close any of these three by coding a guess. When a
codified rule exists, implement it and remove that item from this
list.
